course: dictionary
lesson: 10079
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Theatre is a good example. «Go to the theatre» means a building where people watch plays and shows. The clues are the words around it.
explain: Read the words around the word first. «An operating theatre is a room in a hospital where doctors do operations.» The word hospital and the word doctors tell you that this theatre is a room, not a stage.
explain: Then test your meaning. Put it into the sentence in place of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you have probably got it right.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Theatre» means a building where people watch plays, musicals, dances or shows on a stage.
fact: «Theatre» can also mean the work of writing and acting in plays.
fact: An «operating theatre» is a room in a hospital where doctors do operations.
fact: In the USA the spelling is «theater», and a «movie theater» is a cinema.
exercise: «An operating theatre is a room in a hospital where doctors do operations.» What is an operating theatre? | A stage with red curtains | A classroom for maths | *A room in a hospital where doctors do operations | A type of cinema seat
exercise: «The theatre has 10 rows with 20 seats in each row.» How many seats are there in total? | 10 | 30 | *200 | 2
exercise: «Her theatre career began when she was ten.» In this sentence, what does theatre mean? | A row of seats | *The work of writing and acting in plays | A hospital room | A ticket office
test: Jayden buys a «theatre ticket» for the school play. What does he buy? | A ticket for the library | A ticket to see a doctor | *A ticket to watch a play or show on a stage | A ticket to fly on a plane
test: Ella from America says, «I went to the movie theater on Saturday.» Where did she go? | A library to borrow books | A hospital to see a doctor | *A cinema to watch a film | A stage to do an operation
exam: Which spelling is the US spelling of theatre? | *theater | theatree | theatre | theatra
